<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polans (eastern)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Polianians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polans were an East Slavic tribe of the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a>, living around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a> in the 8th to 10th centuries. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> describes them as a peaceful people who paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazars</a> before falling under the rule of the Rus' princes. Their land became the core of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polans-eastern.jpg" alt="Polans (eastern)" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SeikoEn · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East_Slavic_tribes_peoples_8th_9th_century.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
